I left out the `http-client` import and the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0`, and that clause is the node's entire authority. A platform approval mentioned in the request does not change the grant. Sending the digest text to `metadata.internal.example` would also send the content to a host the node was not granted. Once the graph definition actually includes `aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0` in the `with` clause, the import and fetch can be added.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{digest, published-digest};

    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(composed: digest) -> published-digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::notifier;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        let message = format!("Digest {}: {}", composed.date, composed.overview);
        let published = notifier::notify(&message);
        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
